# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. They are executed inside Linux
# containers (see spec/Dockerfile and compose.yml), and a CRLF shebang makes
# the kernel fail with a confusing "no such file or directory" on the
# interpreter rather than the script. With core.autocrlf=true on Windows these
# files would otherwise be checked out as CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf
